{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-cartan-hadamard","title":"thm:pet-ch6-cartan-hadamard","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.md","line":187,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex#thm:pet-ch6-cartan-hadamard","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-jacobi-field]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-jacobi-dexp-relation]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","label":"thm:pet-ch6-cartan-hadamard","line":502,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[Hadamard--Cartan diffeomorphism theorem]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch6-cartan-hadamard}\n\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0257}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering, def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds}\n  \\dcref{ch6:6.2.2}\n  If $(M,g)$ is complete, connected, and has $\\sec\\le0$, then the universal\n  cover of $M$ is diffeomorphic to $\\mathbb{R}^n$.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch6-jacobi-field, rem:pet-ch6-jacobi-dexp-relation, lem:pet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering}\n  \\sketch\n  For \\(J(0)=0,\\dot J(0)=w\\ne0\\), \\((|J|^2/2)''=|\\dot J|^2-g(R(J,\\dot c)\\dot c,J)\\ge|\\dot J|^2\\). Thus \\(J(1)\\ne0\\), so \\(\\exp_p\\) is nonsingular; \\cref{lem:pet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering} gives the universal cover \\(T_pM\\cong\\mathbb R^n\\).\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[Hadamard--Cartan diffeomorphism theorem] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368362d63617274616e2d686164616d617264\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0257</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23lem%3Apet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering\">↗ lem:pet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23def%3Apet-ch6-sec-bounds\">↗ def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch6:6.2.2</span></span>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> is complete, connected, and has <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sec \\le 0$\">$\\sec \\le 0$</span>, then the universal cover of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is diffeomorphic to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathbb {R}^n$\">$\\mathbb {R}^n$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23def%3Apet-ch6-jacobi-field\">↗ def:pet-ch6-jacobi-field</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23rem%3Apet-ch6-jacobi-dexp-relation\">↗ rem:pet-ch6-jacobi-dexp-relation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23lem%3Apet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering\">↗ lem:pet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering</a> \\sketch For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J(0)=0,\\dot J(0)=w\\ne 0$\">$J(0)=0,\\dot J(0)=w\\ne 0$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(|J|^2/2)&#x27;&#x27;=|\\dot J|^2-g(R(J,\\dot c)\\dot c,J)\\ge |\\dot J|^2$\">$(|J|^2/2)&#x27;&#x27;=|\\dot J|^2-g(R(J,\\dot c)\\dot c,J)\\ge |\\dot J|^2$</span>. Thus <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J(1)\\ne 0$\">$J(1)\\ne 0$</span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p$\">$\\exp _p$</span> is nonsingular; <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23lem%3Apet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368362d6e6f6e73696e67756c61722d6578702d636f766572696e67\">section 2</a> gives the universal cover <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pM\\cong \\mathbb R^n$\">$T_pM\\cong \\mathbb R^n$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-cartan-hadamard-fails-ricci","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering","title":"lem:pet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering","label":"lem:pet-ch6-nonsingular-exp-covering"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds","title":"def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds","label":"def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprin